TimeScale [SimTalk]
Sets the time scale of the GanttChart designated by <Path>. Plant Simulation applies this value when
opening the GanttChart.
Remarks
The unit of the time scale is logical pixels per second. For a time scale of 0.5 Plant Simulation shows a
Gantt event with a duration of 60 seconds with a bar of a length of 30 logical pixels.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.TimeScale:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type real.
Specify 0 to use the default time scaling.
Example
MyGanttChart.TimeScale := 2.5
See also
Show Chart [button] - GanttChart
SankeyDiagram
SankeyDiagram [object]
Use the object SankeyDiagram for visualizing the Sankey flows of parts, the Sankey flows of Workers, who
walk freely within the area or walk on FootPaths, and the Sankey flows of AGVs driving freely within the
area of the model.
